    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="caddb9f7-359e-54b9-b00a-a7cfe5268bcd" activityNameId="e97048a5-dece-5d02-8631-a981d1c24c51" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx Calcium chloride, from hypochlorination of allyl chloride, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx Calcium chloride, from hypochlorination of allyl chloride, at plant
Allyl chloride is reacted  with hylochlorous acid and calcium chloride to produce epichlorohydrin, calcium chloride and water;
UUID: fa36a896-ca52-3084-b061-286a4bb766d5
Multi-output process that produces 1 kg epichlorohydrin,  l.375 kg calcium chloride, and 18 kg of trichloropropane at plant. Economic allocation with allocation factor of 82.4% to epichlorohydrin, 16.2% to calcium chloride, and 1.4% to trichloropropane..
Location: RER
Technology: based on industry data in the US
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature data 
Extrapolations: Some data are derived from other or unknown plants or have been estimated.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_fa36a896-ca52-3084-b061-286a4bb766d5.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
